                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e9cf5ba-5222-31f6-9cf0-a2961bbb78b4",
                                        "entry_id": "3e6a6316-6214-397b-9c54-c10f814dedf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A system of ethics based on the premise that something's value may be measured by its usefulness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52f33ac4-0f23-3435-8912-a42e427ef8e8",
                                        "entry_id": "3e6a6316-6214-397b-9c54-c10f814dedf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The theory that action should be directed toward achieving the \\\"greatest happiness for the greatest number of people\\\" (hedonistic universalism), or one of various related theories."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77c186f3-7b0c-3f33-8db0-366f28200e45",
                                        "entry_id": "3e6a6316-6214-397b-9c54-c10f814dedf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Practicality, functionality, as opposed to e.g. aesthetics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8675927d-43f6-438c-bcd9-a64bee14d2f1",
                                                "sense_id": "77c186f3-7b0c-3f33-8db0-366f28200e45",
                                                "text": "After a few more concerts, my uneasiness took form: the response seemed only to be to the Interpreter as Performer. The reviews praised her artistry. But I heard few women speak of her as a bridge in communication for deaf women, about her function, her \"utilitarianism.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e9e7b615-037e-4170-b53a-61d47827ba76",
                        "source_entry_id": "ec43a600-c9ae-3040-ab23-219f844ac17d",
                        "source_sense_description": "направление в этике, согласно которому моральная ценность поведения или поступка определяется его полезностью",
                        "target_lang_word": "utilitarismo",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "utilitarismo",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b29b8642-5ba7-3676-bb01-11aa4810707f",
                                        "entry_id": "19063ad2-26d4-3eec-9d5f-23d79d7460f1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Doctrina moral y filosófica que juzga el valor de las acciones por la utilidad —medida variadamente como el placer, el bienestar o la felicidad— que producen como consecuencia, no sólo para el autor de la misma sino para el conjunto de los seres racionales. Se opone por lo tanto a toda forma de moral categórica o deontológica, en la que determinados actos poseen valores intrínsecos e independientes de su contexto de realización."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7d52414-c2b6-379b-be17-b1a21072dda1",
                                        "entry_id": "19063ad2-26d4-3eec-9d5f-23d79d7460f1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En general, doctrina que promueve la utilidad como criterio básico de juicio."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9c593c26-7e3c-4b00-a13a-f439ffaf40c9",
